WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.000
That Kai sneaked out of the hotel <i>again</i>.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.340
He doesn't know what teamwork is, does he?

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:51.330
You have no right to say that,
waking up after everyone had already left.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.560
At the very least, he did leave us a note this time.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.710
"There's something I want to investigate.
Don't let me keep you. Move along, now."

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.650
Yeah, I'll move on, alright!

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.980
No, we can't! We have no idea as to what awaits us.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.520
Max has gone shopping,

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.750
and Rei has gone visit one of his old acquaintances.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:19.500
Staying in the hotel room to
wait for Kai would be a waste of time.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.150
So why are you, someone who only cares for science and technology, going to the Louvre?

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.260
You see...

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:30.930
Does it have something to do with powering up our Beyblades?

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:34.260
The Louvre holds the greatest
masterpieces Paris has to offer!

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.000
Greatest masterpieces?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:36.600
Yes!

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:40.360
When did you even find the time to study that stuff?

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:45.770
The Elegant Sacred Beast User

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.080
Go!

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.050
Do it!

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.070
Go! Go!

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.580
Alright!

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.880
Yeah! That's it!

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.000
Go! Keep going!

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.750
I have a question for you.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.820
A question for us?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.880
You're a Blader, right?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.770
Then you know the proper way to ask a question!

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.220
Looks like I was right in coming here.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.390
I'll get this over with quickly.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:36.800
How can you say it's too spicy?!
It's Szechuan shrimp! Of course it's spicy...

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.610
If you don't know your Chinese
cuisine, then don't order at random.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.760
Still muttering to yourself, I see.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.660
Rei!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.490
Long time no see, old man.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.010
Guys, Rei's come to visit!

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.080
What?

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.030
Really?

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.000
Rei!

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.210
Long time no see.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.080
How have you been, Rei?

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.230
You've grown a bit since we last saw you.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.940
<i>Fantastic!</i> Look at all these
cool Beys that aren't sold in Japan...

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.410
I want them all.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.920
Whoa! All of this is the museum?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:26.870
The Louvre is comprised of three wings; Richelieu,
Denon, and Sully, and hosts more than 300,000 works of art.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.390
It's one of the world's largest museums.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.440
That's too bad.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.120
We came all the way here..!

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.150
What?! Reserved?!

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:45.150
Yes. Unfortunately, the whole museum has
been reserved by a Olivier Polange for the day.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.560
Olivier? Where have I heard that name before...

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.900
Are you kidding me?! He's the boy we met yesterday at the Eiffel Tower!

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.630
Not bad.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.590
Allowed to reserve the Louvre just
for himself... Who in the world <i>is</i> he?

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.320
Not to mention his connection to Team Shadows...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.470
It doesn't matter. Anyone that'd reserve a
museum for only them is not a nice person!

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:13.130
Makes me want to get back at him. In fact, I will!

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.080
You're the type of person who wants things they
can't have, no matter how unnecessary, aren't you?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.300
Yeah, exactly! How'd you know?

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.850
You're way too simple-minded...

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.840
Didn't you hear what I said? The museum is reserved.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.910
Come on. Let me in, even if it's for a second.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.880
I can't do that. 'Reserved'
means I can't let other people in.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.770
Then call that Olivier guy over.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.630
I can't do that, either.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:38.610
Why not?!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.620
He asked me not to disturb
him until he left the museum.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.120
Whoa! The Eiffel Tower is
piercing a flying Arc de Triomphe!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.280
Ah, Takao!

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.000
H-Hold it right there!

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.510
Oh? This is the same Olivier we met yesterday.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:02.070
Yep, Olivier Polange. A young
gentleman from one of France's richest families.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.120
You didn't know?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.010
A young gentleman..?

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.010
Ah! There you are!

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:14.070
Hey, it's you.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.190
So you're still in France, Kinomiya Takao-kun?

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:21.280
How did you make it in? Security
stopped you at the entrance, right?

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.240
Who cares about that?! Listen, you...

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.280
Please. My name is Olivier Polange.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.840
Please quit this "you, you" nonsense.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.200
Okay then, Olivier...

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.230
I'm caling you Takao-<i>kun</i>—shouldn't you do the same?

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:37.990
-kun!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:38.800
What is it?

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.880
Why would you reserve this huge museum all for yourself?

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.770
There are lots of people who want to come here!

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.950
I can't appreciate the exposition
with flocks of people walking around.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.530
And that's why you reserved the museum?

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:53.320
Yes.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.780
How selfish can you be?!

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.200
I don't really know what you're trying
to say here, but if I've upset you, I apologize.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.920
Hey, where are you off to now?!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.160
I'll treat you to a restaurant.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.630
Really? Treat me? Aaah!

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:13.720
Takao!

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.600
Why you..!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.160
It's okay.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.680
He's with me.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:21.170
Did you two make up in there?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.680
Well, I don't quite get it, but he's
treating me to lunch as an apology.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.680
Professor-kun, come along.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.560
R-Right...

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.380
What are you doing, Professor? Hurry up!

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.940
Wait for me, Olivier<i>-kun</i>!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:44.170
And I still can't get into the Louvre...

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.960
It really has been a while. Will you
be staying here in Paris for some time?

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.750
No, I'll be heading out before long.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.970
A wanderer through and through, eh?

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.980
Is Beyblade really all that fun?

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:00.460
I think you'd make a great cook.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:04.850
As much as I love cooking, it doesn't compare to Beyblade.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.480
It's everything to me.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.250
That's another part of you that hasn't changed.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:11.520
Oh, this?

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.670
It's an article on last year's cooking
competition. Any kind of cuisine was allowed,

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.480
but as you'd expect, French cuisine came out on top here.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.060
Who's in that picture?

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.070
Ah, that's Olivier Polange, the winner.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.830
He works at his father's restaurant, one
of the highest-rated in France, as vice-chef.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.570
Chef?

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:37.830
Yum, yum! French food ain't all that bad.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:42.830
Takao, French cuisine shouldn't be eaten so carelessly...

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.920
Is that so?

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:52.290
It is so. <i>Entrée, poisson</i>, <i>viande</i>,<i> legume</i>,  <i>fromage</i>,<i> dessert</i>... You eat one at a time.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.070
Ya lost me.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:09:00.690
The appetizer, fish, meat, vegetables, cheese,
and dessert. Together, they form a full-course meal.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.980
Come on, what's it matter to ya? It's tasty!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.680
I knew you'd say that.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.870
Could you at least eat more slowly?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:09.700
Why?

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.610
We stand out enough as-is!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.570
Oh... I kinda get what you mean now.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.450
Pay it no mind.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:25.710
You're my guests. If you want, I can
ask all of the others customers to leave.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.950
No, no! We're okay!

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.040
Professor, you worry too much!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.100
And you worry way too little!

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.950
How are you enjoying my cooking?

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.980
What? You made all of this?

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:40.990
Yep.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:43.190
It's delish! Ten outta ten!

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:45.700
You're a funny guy.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:52.480
I was wondering what type of
Bladers were entering the World Finals,

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.280
but someone like you didn't exactly come to mind.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.520
I know, right?

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.200
Professor!

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:01.710
Still, Takao is strong. Much stronger than you can imagine.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.710
Is that so? Want to give it a try?

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.220
Give what a try?

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.860
You're last up.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.230
Why you..!

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.830
Now tell me.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.880
Have you ever seen one of Olivier Polange's matches?

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.890
What are we going to do out here?

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:57.130
The <i>Jardin du Luxembourg</i> is the
most beautiful place in Paris, in my opinion.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.230
That's not what I'm asking...

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:03.200
Raising one's voice demonstrates a lack of self-confidence.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.970
Cadav was that way, too.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.250
Cadav!

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.870
So you really are related to Team Shadows!

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:12.640
Oh, please. I think you've misinterpreted things.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:16.110
I simply went up against Cadav in the Tournament.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.640
I have nothing to do with those guys.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:19.800
Is that so..?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.960
Then you're the one Cadav lost to, aren't you?

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:27.710
Of course. How could I ever lose to a guy with no Sacred Beast?

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.720
Does that mean you have a Sacred Beast, too?

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.430
My Sacred Beast is a sight to see.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.630
We're here.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.940
This is my Bey training ground.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:43.940
Eh?!

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:53.600
Now, show me what power goes beyond my imagination!

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.970
Rei! It's really you!

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:14.850
Oh, Max!

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:20.120
Wow! You had lunch at this <i>very,
very</i> expensive-looking restaurant?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.840
No. Apparently Olivier, the guy we met yesterday, is a chef here.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:28.310
Chef?! <i>No, no!</i> Olivier is a
young gentleman from a rich family!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.360
That's what the guy at the newsstand told me.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:34.340
I heard from a friend of mine that's a cook.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.430
He would know.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.920
Olivier Polange is fighting!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.510
What, for real?

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:43.680
Yeah! Let's see the French Beyblade
Champion fight for the first time in ages!

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.550
"French Beyblade Champion"?

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.120
Yup.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.650
What the heck? Why are all
these people surrounding us?

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.350
They've come to appreciate my battle.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:01.350
To appreciate?

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.590
Yes. My battles are a work of art.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:08.980
What are you even saying? A battle is a battle.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.990
Well, I can't expect someone like you, who fights like a barbarian, to understand.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.440
Like a barbarian..?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.590
Argh! That's an awful way to put it!

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:23.220
Enough chitchat! Get ready to fight!

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.790
I'll blow you out!

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:30.390
Sure. I'll give you a taste of my art.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.210
Let's go!

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:39.560
Three, Two, One!

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.520
Go... Shoot!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.380
Go, Dragoon!

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:53.030
Your fighting style has no composure.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:53.650
What?!

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:57.200
There's no beauty to a hasty style.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.580
This is the way I fight!

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:13.040
He's easily dodging Dragoon's
attacks, which surely aren't slow!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.800
His technique is incredible!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.800
All bark and no bite, all you do is run!

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.110
Don't lose, Dragoon!

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.490
I will allow you to enjoy my full course!

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:32.730
First, the <i>entrée</i>. A little exercise to stimulate the appetite.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.370
Get outta there, Dragoon!

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.130
Next,<i> poisson</i>, <i>viande</i>,<i> legume</i>!

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:48.800
Please enjoy the balance of these three dishes.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:53.070
You..! Don't get ahead of
yourself because you're a bit fast!

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.040
Dragoon!

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:58.510
Take this! Dragoon Phantom!

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:17.590
Like yesterday, your control of
the Sacred Beast is no good whatsoever.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:19.580
Unicolyon!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.440
This is..!

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:37.680
Are they from the same species?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.180
What?

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:51.320
That light..!

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.440
It's the light of a Sacred Beast!

00:15:55.440 --> 00:16:00.600
No way! That huge, bright
light is that of a Sacred Beast?!

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:11.920
Dragoon is losing rotational speed!

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.290
W-What's up with you, Dragoon?!

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:19.960
A Sacred Beast only becomes
useful if you master its control.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:23.800
Merely summoning it won't have you compete with me.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.720
Not yet! The battle's not over yet!

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:32.310
Oh, you still have the strength to
go on? Even with your Bey like this?

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:36.320
What do I do? What can I do now?!

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:43.610
Olivier!

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.880
It's huge. It's way too big!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:47.960
What can I..?

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.630
Takao! What are you doing?!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.300
Max! Rei!

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:55.770
This battle is far from over!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.180
Why lose all hope when Dragoon most needs you?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.310
Don't tell me you're giving up now!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:07.050
Y-You idiot! There's no way I'd ever give up!

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:13.010
They're right... What the heck am I
doing?! My partner is still doing his best!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.810
The real fight starts now, Olivier!

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:19.830
Looks like you're the type who never learns.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:23.120
All the easier to crush you until you won't get up again!

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.360
I won't give up so easily!

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:28.750
You're bluffing so hard it's but a sad sight.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:30.870
Unicolyon!

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:33.630
Crush him!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.190
Hold on, Dragoon!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.220
Futile.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:49.880
And now the finisher! <i>Fromage</i> and <i>dessert</i>!

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.560
Go! Dragoon!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:01.700
With every last ounce of your energy, awaken!

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:04.780
What..?

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.590
I-It's beautiful...

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:18.580
Phantom Hurricane!

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:24.600
Don't let your guard dowwn, Kinomiya!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.670
Unicolyon still has its horn!

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:59.170
He managed to tie with Olivier...

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.530
Even so, Olivier almost had it.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.090
Yeah, he just got unlucky.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.100
Stop!

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.130
Stop your foolish chatter!

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.780
How strong...

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.130
Amazing!

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:22.060
You really must be strong to draw with me.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:26.150
Rejecting the result would be an unsightly thing to do.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:29.200
I still can't accept this!

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:33.010
Someone as incredibly strong as
you is going to be in the Finals, right?

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:34.950
Let's settle our score then!

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:36.590
No, I won't be there.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.360
Why?!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:40.000
I don't like fighting in groups.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:43.090
It's also clear as day that we're the best in the world.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.040
<i>We're</i> the best..?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:50.480
The four Bladers that represent Europe.
We're all outstanding Sacred Beast users.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:53.070
Some of them are even stronger than me.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.800
No way!

00:19:54.800 --> 00:20:00.360
Right. One of them is in Italy.
An interesting fellow for sure.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.320
You should go and fight him.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.980
That way, you'll come to know Europe's power.

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:08.820
Did he also fight against Team Shadows, by any chance?

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.370
Yep, good guess!

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:14.270
He fought against Phan.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.440
Well then.

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.720
Professor, how'd you know that?

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:26.880
Team Shadow started hating the Sacred
Beasts after being defeated by Sacred Beast users.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.500
And Cadav lost to Olivier...

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:32.100
So I put two and two together.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.500
What were you talking about?

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.230
He told us to go to Italy.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.840
Huh? Where's Kai?

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:42.680
Not here. He left looking for answers.

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.680
I was sure I heard his voice back there...

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:48.100
Oh? Then he might have been hanging around.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:52.400
You know how he is. He's
probably here, pretending not to care.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.380
I can see that.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.540
Anyway... Next stop, Italy!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.690
You've decided to go because Olivier told you to?!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:04.650
He said there's a powerful opponent there.
There's no way I could let that pass me by!

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:08.910
<i>Yes!</i> We're training, so we
need a strong opponent to fight!

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.380
Right?

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:14.140
It's fine, isn't it? It's not like
we'd be making a huge detour.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.430
Then it's decided!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.930
I can see more troubles on the horizon...

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:23.840
What are you saying? I'm getting
all excited just thinking about it!

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.460
Right, Rei? Max?

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:26.100
Right.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:27.170
<i>Yes!</i>

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:32.190
How can you lot be so easy-going?! Seriously!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:02.110
According to my analysis, our next opponent looks very strong!

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:06.400
Or so I was going to say, but
he's a womanizer and a skirt-chaser.

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:11.000
He's so terrible that I feel terrible just mentioning it!

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:17.200
But in reality, he's descends from the Roman
Empire, and controls the Sacred Beast Amphilyon!

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:20.510
Next time: Duel at the <i>Colosseo</i>!

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:24.060
To tell you the truth, I'm quite jealous of him.
